    reg {
        name = "DDR operating mode register";
        desc = "DDRC_CFG_DDRMODE is a DDR operating mode register.

Vendor U-Boot (stock flash image) writes 0x15 for a 16-bit DDR2: dram_type = 5 (DDR2), mem_width = 1 (16 bit), brstlen = 0 (BL4). The data sheet init procedure (4.1.4.3 step 5) prints 0x25 for the same configuration, which would be mem_width = 2 (32 bit): data sheet typo.

Data sheet 4.1.6 DDRC_CFG_DDRMODE (offset 0x50, printed page 4-51, dump line 34406).

Hardware (Hi3518E V200 board, live dump): reads 0x00000015 (dram_type 5 = DDR2, mem_width 1 = 16 bit, brstlen 0 = BL4, rank 0 = 1 rank). This is the value the vendor register table writes; the DDR type is not sensed by hardware, software reads back what it programmed (the 'last digit 5 = DDR2, 6 = DDR3' rule of the OpenIPC README).";

        enum DDRC_CFG_DDRMODE_rank_enum {
            V_1_RANK = 0 { name = "V 1 Rank"; desc = "1 rank"; };
            V_2_RANKS = 1 { name = "V 2 Ranks"; desc = "2 ranks"; };
            V_3_RANKS = 2 { name = "V 3 Ranks"; desc = "3 ranks"; };
            V_4_RANKS = 3 { name = "V 4 Ranks"; desc = "4 ranks"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "rank";
            desc = "DDRC rank";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = DDRC_CFG_DDRMODE_rank_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } rank[21:20];

        enum DDRC_CFG_DDRMODE_odt_on_enum {
